    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the $3.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line on trip TRP-02816 is unmatched by the GPS trace (nearest fix 330.73 m, outside the 250 m crossing radius) and is refunded as a standalone billing-integrity correction; record this as a billing-integrity finding."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The rider disputed a $3.00 ERP charge for a road the trip never used. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02816) carries exactly one ERP line, 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', at $3.00, and the platform's own comparison of that gantry's coordinates (lat 1.289647, lng 103.863838) against the driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02816) shows the closest the vehicle ever came was 330.73 m, at 11:10:50. POL-RD-09 treats a fix within 250 m of a gantry as a crossing; 330.73 m is outside that radius, so the trace never passes this gantry. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure and is refunded in full as a standalone correction, whether or not a deviation exists. The $3.00 is therefore returned to the rider, and the case is recorded for billing-integrity review. This is a PARTIAL_REFUND: it returns the contested ERP line only, not the whole fare.\n\nThe driver's answer — 'the ERP is charged by the system' — is no defence to this correction. It names no gantry, road or evidence, carries no weight, and cannot show the vehicle crossed a gantry the trace places 330.73 m away.\n\nThe distance and time charges are left standing. On the trace the driven distance is 20.58 km against the 19.6 km optimal route — an excess of 0.98 km, or 5.00%. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be both more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km; the percentage test fails, so no deviation is established, no POL-RD-02 recomputation runs, and the driver keeps the metered distance and time charges for the 20.58 km, 26.8-minute trip.\n\nNo repeat-deviation or conduct finding arises. The driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 395 completed trips in 90 days, so no POL-RD-06 pattern is established and no POL-RD-06(c) referral issues; the lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags and prior_deviation_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and are not used. The rider's profile likewise bars nothing and demands no extra corroboration (1 claim in 60 days, 0 substantiated). The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes — 162 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps — trip identifiers match across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown (TRP-02816), and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires.\n\nFigures used: charged_total $30.55 (EV-FARE-02816); ERP line $3.00; optimal distance 19.6 km and trace distance 20.58 km (EV-GPS-02816); nearest fix 330.73 m. The ruling rests on the fare breakdown and the GPS trace, both at full weight 1.0. Its monetary effect, $3.00, is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes on issue. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
