    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is upheld in part. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02816) carries exactly one ERP line — 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', charged 2026-08-30T10:58:30, $3.00 — flagged on_optimal_route = false against an optimal-route ERP total of $0.00. The platform's derived gantry-proximity check on the driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02816) puts the nearest fix to that gantry at 330.73 m (fix index 128, 2026-08-30T11:10:50), with no bracketing of the closest approach. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace only where a fix falls within 250 m of it; 330.73 m is outside that radius, so the trace never passes this gantry. That is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction available whether or not a deviation exists. Refund: $3.00, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 — still $3.00. To the driver: no distance or time refund is ordered. POL-RD-01 measures the excess on the trace at 0.98 km / 5.00% against a booked optimal of 19.6 km; establishment requires the excess to be BOTH greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km, and 5.00% fails the first test, so no deviation is established and your metered fare stands. POL-RD-02 therefore does not run, and the $3.83 gap between charged_total of $30.55 and a recomputed fare of $26.72 (which would include no on-optimal-route ERP) is not payable as a distance refund; the $3.00 pass-through correction is the only refund, so nothing is double-counted. Your statement that 'the ERP is charged by the system' cites no evidence ID and no clause; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and does not show the vehicle crossed the gantry. Claims answered: the ERP billing-integrity claims from both sides are accepted and set the $3.00 refund; the POL-RD-01 no-deviation claims from both sides are accepted, so no distance or time refund; the profile claims are accepted — driver deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 395 completed trips in 90 days, so no POL-RD-06 pattern, no full-refund uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises, and rider deviation_claims_60d is 1 with 0 substantiated, so no corroboration beyond the trace is required; the lifetime counters prior_deviation_flags, prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed and prior_disputes_upheld are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used; the trace-integrity claims are accepted — 162 fixes, 10 s sampling, 100.0% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0, so no POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment; and the escalation-avoidance claims are accepted. Impairment and confidence: the deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-02816 (weight 1.0) and EV-FARE-02816 (weight 1.0); no artifact below weight 1.0 carries any part of the finding. EV-ADVIS-02816-01 (TRAFFIC_ADVISORY) is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT and carries nothing; the two claims resting on it were discarded by the referee for non-disclosure of that impairment. Confidence is capped at 1.0 and set at 0.90. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers all read TRP-02816, the pickup timestamp 2026-08-30T10:49:30 agrees across the trace and the trip record, no timestamps run backwards, the trace is not impaired, the refund is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total, and the only unmatched charge line is the ERP line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excludes. The referral below is an addition to the money ruling, not an escalation. Because the monetary effect does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), it executes automatically on issue."
